Place `DotCanvas` inside a `relative` container. It fills the parent with a dotted grid and ignores
pointer events, so content above stays interactive. The overlay is decorative and hidden from
assistive technology.

```svelte
<script lang="ts">
  import { DotCanvas } from '~/lib/dot-canvas';
</script>

<div class="relative h-48 overflow-hidden rounded-xl border">
  <DotCanvas />
  <p class="relative z-10 p-6 text-sm">Content sits above the dots.</p>
</div>
```

Pass `size` as `12`, `20`, or `24` (default) to change grid pitch. Use `class` for opacity,
masks, or placement overrides.

```svelte
<DotCanvas size={12} class="mask-[radial-gradient(ellipse_at_center,transparent_20%,black_85%)]" />
```
